#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192615 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de6c0f2-b9c3-518d-ba86-40ec3fcbd4f3" :knowledge-point/title "Measuring Angles Using a Protractor"}] :question/id #uuid "55e26a5c-18da-5923-a45f-f5cdaed73ac2" :question/math-academy-id "e-2576" :question/problem "Determine the measure of the angles shown below.\n\n![](images/8a/8a74f14be370f7ca987cd5271572477f4e15a91f54be9ad662ec1455af7c4183.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use a protractor to determine the measure of the angles.\n\nTo do this, we align one side of an angle with the zero mark (on the left or on the right side of the protractor) and read the degrees where the second side of the angle intersects the scale of numbers:\n\nBy doing this, we get the following angle measures.\n\n![](images/0b/0bf274dff799a9b7695c0e8dfc5f3850ac9c196f94d3ffb0210fc1df1bf12386.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192616 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42452f6-bf63-5c2e-a4d0-4ed5f6124c91" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Angle Measure by Taking a Difference"}] :question/id #uuid "76f4a24f-4d7b-5be8-a86a-b1ae86c9f991" :question/math-academy-id "e-2589" :question/problem "Determine the measure of the angle $\\angle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/feb2c7d5645b1443194baabcf4f7153fe15cb8059e4f590e2ee30a3a80a29aef.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the angle, we can use either scale of the protractor. \n\n- First, let's use the upper scale. The side $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ of the angle intersects the upper scale at $125^\\circ,$ and the other side $\\overrightarrow{BC}$ intersects the upper scale at $20^\\circ.$ To find the measure of $\\angle ABC,$ we subtract the smaller reading from the larger one and get\n\n$$\nm\\angle ABC = 125^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 105^\\circ.\n$$\n\n- If we use the lower scale, we get the same result. The side $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ of the angle intersects the lower scale at $55^\\circ,$ and the other side $\\overrightarrow{BC}$ intersects the lower scale at $160^\\circ.$ Subtracting the smaller reading from the larger one,  we get \n\n$$\nm\\angle ABC = 160^\\circ - 55^\\circ = 105^\\circ.\n$$\n\nWe can check our result by rotating the protractor to align its zero with the side $\\overrightarrow{BC},$ as shown below. This way, we can perform the usual process, taking only a single measurement. Indeed, we see that $m\\angle ABC$ is equal to $105^\\circ.$\n\n![](images/02/0292b94168d618a8fe48b47c524b71b5b3ca40fa42c89f104b2b8eca10f3a847.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de6c0f2-b9c3-518d-ba86-40ec3fcbd4f3" :knowledge-point/title "Measuring Angles Using a Protractor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e4df4e-d39b-5b78-9c05-bbb663084bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454994} {:answer/id #uuid "68099440-cc10-5eeb-802b-49fcdbdbdd3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{114}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455095} {:answer/id #uuid "90a9c60b-8c29-51f0-b055-60a12882d809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455165} {:answer/id #uuid "b61d3034-4ca8-54b1-9c83-c0a580b12639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{130}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455222} {:answer/id #uuid "e144ca4a-7486-5c6d-a47d-b577c448ec3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{118}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90a9c60b-8c29-51f0-b055-60a12882d809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455165} :answer-field/id #uuid "4352e214-a796-5703-a843-0c023f66dc67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa2e299b-8053-575c-a445-dc3a8b58a009" :question/math-academy-id "q-40668" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb3c9b1a249cfd2b6f13e2e7b3a731549094b7e6ea38432d5dcd000a7083f7ec.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of the angle $∠ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use a protractor to determine the measure of the angle $∠ABC.$ \n\nTo do this, we read the degrees where the side $\\overset{\\to }{BA}$ of the angle intersects the scale of numbers:\n\n![](images/8a/8a89b7b52135983b18892d07e173b95d7afdcc1efaa4b9c91fb0013b26d279fc.png)\n\nTherefore, we have that $m∠ABC={120}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42452f6-bf63-5c2e-a4d0-4ed5f6124c91" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Angle Measure by Taking a Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33853608-df2b-5f3a-bd95-41007a3ca59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454983} {:answer/id #uuid "4735a64e-631f-5c39-8793-f8b8a61f81b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455022} {:answer/id #uuid "92c68e62-b5be-5bc4-b448-ed03197d98ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{115}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455170} {:answer/id #uuid "f99f6238-b56e-5ca6-b210-bcfd26ccec6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455331} {:answer/id #uuid "fa22d818-a336-5d4e-8ad9-61380c84d712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f99f6238-b56e-5ca6-b210-bcfd26ccec6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455331} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee8faa67-ddf4-569a-85c6-7a39ea90245d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef364631-7848-5586-9790-7f94e2b665da" :question/math-academy-id "q-52640" :question/problem "![](images/cc/ccda9a0334c7981def5e4a3f96cc6a22c9e71cc1218b8e1b6dc8084f08abbffa.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of the angle $∠ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let's use the upper scale of the protractor.\n\n- The side $\\overset{\\to }{BA}$ of the angle intersects the upper scale of numbers at ${145}^{∘}.$\n\n- The side $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ intersects the upper scale of numbers at ${65}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the measure of $∠ABC,$ we subtract the smaller reading from the larger one and get\n\n$$\nm∠ABC={145}^{∘}-{65}^{∘}={80}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42452f6-bf63-5c2e-a4d0-4ed5f6124c91" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Angle Measure by Taking a Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271dcc17-2ff6-5173-b579-1075c7c12045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{130}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454963} {:answer/id #uuid "500faa85-30ff-5a81-8701-0aaf933abee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455045} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf8992c-3a7c-5019-8e5e-567463c359ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{125}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455229} {:answer/id #uuid "d2885676-49d4-5b94-932e-23c1f8357f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455269} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0e349b-fb9b-55b3-95c0-d1aaa22c312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271dcc17-2ff6-5173-b579-1075c7c12045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{130}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e75af724-7be8-5b79-9cea-68486db5a721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb2c238d-772a-5f5c-a9d1-ab3e5d8e865b" :question/math-academy-id "q-67608" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7cda3efc4a07a69c5cd389b59bb0ef18b55b5e58d38405cf211ea27e7dab4a5.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of the angle $∠ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let's use the upper scale of the protractor.\n\n- The side $\\overset{\\to }{BA}$ of the angle intersects the upper scale of numbers at ${25}^{∘}.$\n\n- The side $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ intersects the upper scale of numbers at ${155}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the measure of $∠ABC,$ we subtract the smaller reading from the larger one and get\n\n$$\nm∠ABC={155}^{∘}-{25}^{∘}={130}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de6c0f2-b9c3-518d-ba86-40ec3fcbd4f3" :knowledge-point/title "Measuring Angles Using a Protractor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47e3813d-4760-542a-bdb8-1e683b99e5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5485a82694a9ee09a899f1241c86ac6eff6183b6d3f4d35b02d8181e627e4f5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455024} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd40f8e-5abf-59d3-951a-5bc8af46779c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/61cee5d33e790e706c7163148cd9bd796a324b2b0f5fa48dd7bf8021c1805262.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455071} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0f0c06-aad0-5fcf-a3b8-00e296abbd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f50d8c951cbb2b9b892fbb96116adb302176d6bcbe0d9ff1ca86f66927df9bd1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455101} {:answer/id #uuid "d7250ae1-ea84-57d5-b071-f7ab19f1dc6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/03db38618f2783fd5ca8508846b222b40302dc1bb3702e45395e6435cc9c5e01.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455280} {:answer/id #uuid "e55d8952-7ddd-5f3e-ab5d-c8838b85a2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e8d2163643460b4d7ec2e5fa00f8428e39ff1b16066a32743c5d8d775456ec5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b0f0c06-aad0-5fcf-a3b8-00e296abbd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f50d8c951cbb2b9b892fbb96116adb302176d6bcbe0d9ff1ca86f66927df9bd1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455101} :answer-field/id #uuid "24b41f74-df4b-557a-a219-34f9ffdabfc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98ff0e85-1725-5e8f-8655-5aa5679d577c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76712" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c8865e67ff36fe06a6d1cf1be8c591468f1fef98b060ccb404b3bb61509edcf.png)\n\nWhich of the following shows an angle of ${50}^{∘}$ measured on a protractor?" :question/worked-solution "First, consider a ray $\\overset{\\to }{AB}.$\n\n![](images/25/25eb043b8404684ab57632c27b5c1e6addbbd47bd396cda2793f7631b039ee0c.png)\n\nWe place the midpoint of the protractor at the origin of $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ that is, at the point $A.$ Then we align this ray with the line that passes through the midpoint and zero of the protractor.\n\n![](images/b8/b8346376ea89fd1a90ddf244d6f45a9581f5cec231a1c93e94798c83d86e266b.png)\n\nIn the internal scale of the protractor, we locate the mark associated with the given measure (in this case, ${50}^{∘}$) and then we draw a point to the margin of the protractor. We will call this point $C.$\n\n![](images/75/75d979d34a4f05857a1bfba76e1b91e7f6296ae6e9832eaa39fe6fca72ef5282.png)\n\nFinally, we draw the ray $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n![](images/8b/8bdff8e18433abf3b38d99c73cb7cbe9d18b379880cc64b55166c651f2342d96.png)\n\nHence, the angle $∠BAC$ has a measure of ${50}^{∘}.$"}]}
